--- body ---
## Context

The ledger already chunks tables by country and `recorded_at` year. Its
reader only accepts `<CODE>-<year>.csv`, and its writer emits one file per
country-year even when that file exceeds the ceiling. Indonesia's 2026 line
chunk is 509667 bytes before the 0970 rows. Backdating new decisions to
another year, shortening citations until they are imprecise, or crossing the
hook's ceiling would corrupt the storage contract.

## Work

- Permit ordered numeric shards `IDN-2026-02.csv`, `-03.csv` when one
  country-year grows beyond the ceiling; preserve the original unsuffixed
  name for its first shard and numeric read order for later shards.
- Pack the writer's rows without splitting a CSV record; refuse a single
  record that cannot fit with its header and leave unrelated files untouched.
- Document the suffix and verify a split table produces the same SQLite
  ledger as an unsplit table.

## Exit criteria

- [x] Reader rejoins same-year shards in source order and validates country,
  year, header and 512000-byte per-file ceiling.
- [x] Writer packs every shard within the ceiling and cleans only its own
  obsolete shard files after a smaller rewrite.
- [x] The split and unsplit fixtures build byte-identical SQLite ledgers;
  an oversized single row fails before any output is written.
- [x] Focused tests, `make check-fast`, `make lint`, and full `make check`
  run, with any unrelated full-gate failures recorded by test ID.
